    "created_at": "2026-06-10T08:55:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-10T08:55:37Z",
    "body": "I've been looking into this and traced the root cause to `replace_parameter()` in `vllm/model_executor/utils.py` (around L94-96). When `_setup_kernel()` converts the weight buffer from checkpoint layout `[w1;w3]` to kernel layout `[w3;w1]`, the `weight_loader` attribute gets carried over via `replace_parameter()`. On any subsequent `load_weights()` call, the stale `weight_loader` still writes data assuming checkpoint order into a buffer that's already in kernel format — silently corrupting the forward pass.\n\nI noticed #42823 takes a broader approach (making load_weights generally safe for reload), but it seems stalled. My fix is more targeted: clear the `weight_loader` attribute on `w13_weight` and `w2_weight` at the end of `_setup_kernel()` once the kernel format conversion is done. This prevents the stale loader from ever being invoked again without touching the general weight loading path.\n\nI'll put up a PR shortly.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
